Speedup claim
  The frontier-gain table replaces per-candidate unit-edge recounts.
  The displayed speedup is only for edge-count checks; canonicalization
  and beam ordering still cost time, but the expensive count itself
  becomes state-local rather than child-local.
  Next heavy run: increase --width and add automorphism canonicalization
  or bitset popcounts on a bounded Moser window.
